;; X-CATEGORY-ARGMAX (my.data composition gym) — group-then-argmax over a SEEDED
;; expense dataset. A cold agent (never told the schema) is asked which CATEGORY
;; of spending is biggest AND its total — a question no single reduction answers:
;;   - a flat SUM over every row gives 219 (the whole week), wrong question.
;;   - a flat argMAX over the rows gives the $73 Trader Joe's GROCERIES row,
;;     wrong category.
;; Only group-by-category → sum-each → argmax-over-the-groups yields dining@106.
;; That is the my.data pipeline `rows → group-sum → max-by` (or the exact
;; hand-rolled datalog equivalent).
;;
;; SINGLE agent over a SEEDED store (deliberately NOT the x1/x3 A-logs→B-reads
;; shape): a two-turn A→B form double-counts here — pre-seeded fixtures PLUS an
;; agent re-logging the same week mints duplicate entities (:my.expense/merchant
;; is not an identity attr), doubling dining to 212. A controlled composition
;; instrument needs ONE unambiguous dataset, so the rows are seeded and a single
;; agent analyses them. Discovery is preserved — the agent is never told the
;; :my.expense/* kind; it must read the store (the inventory block surfaces the
;; attr, a real read still finds the rows).
;;
;; Mechanical legs anchor on op-FAMILIES + the category attr-name stem
;; (non-fragile); the computed biggest-category + its total live ONLY on the
;; :llm-judge axis. An :eval-error-rate leg also scores REPL cleanliness.
;;
;; PAID — costs real money. Refused without {:seon.gym/allow-paid? true} +
;; the active provider's API key.
{:seon.gym.scenario/id     :x-category-argmax
 :seon.gym.scenario/doc    "A cold agent, never told the :my.expense/* kind, is asked which CATEGORY of a seeded week of spending (dining 106, groceries 73, transport 40) is biggest AND its total. Group-then-argmax — unpassable by a flat sum (219) or a flat max (the $73 groceries row); only rows→group-sum→max-by yields dining@106."
 :seon.gym.scenario/tier   :paid
 :seon.gym.scenario/status :active
 :seon.gym.scenario/competency :db-memory
 :seon.gym.scenario/axes   [:consults-findings :replies-honestly :terminates
                            :makes-few-errors]
 :seon.gym.scenario/schema-registrations
 [[:my.expense/merchant :string]
  [:my.expense/amount-usd :int]
  [:my.expense/category :keyword]]
 ;; dining = 28+52+26 = 106 (biggest); groceries = 73; transport = 40.
 ;; Flat sum of all rows = 219; flat argmax row = Trader Joe's @73 (groceries).
 :seon.gym.scenario/fixtures
 [{:my.expense/merchant "Thai Place"    :my.expense/amount-usd 28 :my.expense/category :dining}
  {:my.expense/merchant "Sushi Bar"     :my.expense/amount-usd 52 :my.expense/category :dining}
  {:my.expense/merchant "Cafe Luna"     :my.expense/amount-usd 26 :my.expense/category :dining}
  {:my.expense/merchant "Trader Joe's"  :my.expense/amount-usd 73 :my.expense/category :groceries}
  {:my.expense/merchant "Shell"         :my.expense/amount-usd 40 :my.expense/category :transport}]
 :seon.gym.scenario/turns
 [{:seon.gym.turn/message "Look at the expenses on file for me — which kind of spending was my biggest this past week, and how much did it come to?"}]
 :seon.gym.scenario/predicates
 [{:seon.gym.predicate/id     :expenses-seeded-visible
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind   :datalog
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis   :consults-findings
   :seon.gym.predicate/query  [:find ?e :where [?e :my.expense/amount-usd _]]
   ;; EXACTLY 5 — a regression that re-introduces the double-count (an agent
   ;; re-logging the seeded week) shows up here as 10, RED, not as a silently
   ;; doubled judge total.
   :seon.gym.predicate/expect [:count 5]}
  ;; AGGREGATION EVIDENCE: the agent grouped the stored rows by category —
  ;; either via the my.data verb (group-sum), Clojure group-by, or a datalog
  ;; grouping that necessarily names :my.expense/category. The alternation
  ;; rewards using the aggregation surface without coaching the answer (a
  ;; correct hand-roll that groups by category still matches). Behavioral.
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id     :grouped-by-category
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind   :eval-count-matching
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis   :consults-findings
   :seon.gym.predicate/pattern "data/group-sum|group-by|:my\\.expense/category"
   :seon.gym.predicate/expect [:count>= 1]}
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id     :replied-to-the-user
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind   :datalog
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis   :replies-honestly
   :seon.gym.predicate/args   [:seon.gym.agent/a]
   :seon.gym.predicate/query  [:find ?m
                               :in $ ?aid
                               :where
                               [?ag :seon.agent/id ?aid]
                               [?m :seon.agent.message/from ?ag]
                               [?m :seon.agent.message/hops ?h]
                               [(pos? ?h)]]
   :seon.gym.predicate/expect :non-empty}
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id     :agent-ends-idle
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind   :datalog
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis   :terminates
   ;; idle is DERIVED, never a stored :seon.agent/state datom: an agent is
   ;; idle iff not terminated and owns NO open run. The single agent idle = 1.
   :seon.gym.predicate/query  [:find ?a
                               :where
                               [?a :seon.agent/id _]
                               (not [?a :seon.agent/terminated-at _])
                               (not-join [?a]
                                 [?r :seon.agent.run/agent ?a]
                                 [?r :seon.agent.run/status :open])]
   :seon.gym.predicate/expect [:count 1]}
  ;; REPL cleanliness on the live drive (curation #44): the failed-eval
  ;; fraction must stay ≤ 0.2 — a composition that fights the API reds here.
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id             :keeps-the-repl-clean
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind           :eval-error-rate
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis           :makes-few-errors
   :seon.gym.predicate/max-error-rate 0.2}
  ;; --- judged answer correctness, the ONLY place the computed values live ---
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id        :judge-biggest-category
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind      :llm-judge
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis      :replies-honestly
   :seon.gym.predicate/rubric    "PASS only if the reply names DINING (eating out / restaurants) as the biggest spending category AND states its total as 106 USD (allow 105-107 for rounding). FAIL if it names a different category (e.g. groceries), omits the total, reports a wrong number, or gives the whole-week total (219) instead of the per-category figure."
   :seon.gym.predicate/reference "Per-category totals: dining 106 (28+52+26), groceries 73, transport 40. Biggest = dining @ 106 — knowable ONLY by grouping the stored rows by category, summing each group, and taking the argmax over the groups. A flat sum of all rows is 219 (wrong); a flat max over the rows is the 73 groceries row (wrong category). A single guessed number cannot land both the exact biggest category AND its exact total."}]}
